            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/filter.py` with a script that removes JavaScript from HTML while preserving all legitimate content and formatting.\n\n**The script handles:**\n- **`<script>` tags**: Removes all script tags and their content (including inline scripts and external script src attributes)\n- **Event handlers**: Removes all `on*` attributes (`onclick`, `onload`, `onerror`, `onmouseover`, etc.) with proper handling of quoted and unquoted values\n- **JavaScript URLs**: Removes `javascript:` protocol from URLs in `href`, `src`, `data`, and `action` attributes\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npython filter.py input.html\n```\n\nThe file is modified in-place. All HTML structure, formatting, tables, headers, and non-dangerous attributes are preserved exactly as-is."
